		(property "Maximum Working Voltage Conditions" "Continuous DC or AC RMS. Lesser of √(P×R) or maximum working voltage. OCPM calculated nominal applied-voltage limit: 2.5 V, from R=100 Ω, P=0.0625 W, and the 50 V manufacturer ceiling. Apply the stated power-rating conditions, derating and resistance tolerance; not an insulation rating."
			(at 0 0 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
		(property "Source Guidance" "The 50 V ceiling is a continuous-working-voltage limit for the resistor element. Source quote: The maximum working voltage that may be continuously applied to the resistor element, see “IEC publication 60115-8” | The applicable continuous working voltage is power-derived and limited by the published maximum working-voltage ceiling. Source quote: The DC or AC (rms) continuous working voltage corresponding to the rated power is determined by the following formula: | The published 50 V value is a continuous-working-voltage ceiling subject to the rated-voltage rule. Source quote: The maximum working voltage that may be continuously applied to the resistor element, see “IEC publication 60115-8”"
			(at 0 0 0)
			(effects
