		(property "Source Guidance" "The 50 V DC rating is the manufacturer's continuous-voltage limit. Source quote: The rated voltage is defined as the maximum voltage which may be applied continuously to the capacitor. | Superimposed AC and DC waveforms must remain within the rated-voltage range using the stated peak criterion. Source quote: When AC voltage is superimposed on DC voltage, V(peak to peak) or V(zero to peak), whichever is larger, should be maintained within the rated voltage range. | For this product rated below 100 V DC, limit body self-heating to below 20°C at 25°C ambient. Source quote: The load should be contained so that the self-heating of the capacitor body remains below 20°C, when measuring at an ambient temperature of 25°C. | The 50 V DC rating is the continuous maximum rated voltage. Source quote: The rated voltage is defined as the maximum voltage which may be applied continuously to the capacitor. | For combined AC and DC excitation, the stated peak measure must remain within the 50 V rating. Source quote: When AC voltage is superimposed on DC voltage, V(peak to peak) or V(zero to peak), whichever is larger, should be maintained within the rated voltage range."
